### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081/api/coupons

### 1. Health check (is the app up and connected to MongoDB?)
GET http://localhost:8081/actuator/health

### 2. Create a coupon -> 201 Created
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "save20",
  "provider": "Amazon",
  "category": "Electronics",
  "description": "20% off on orders over Rs. 2000",
  "discount": 20,
  "expiryDate": "2027-12-31"
}

### 3. Create the same code again -> 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SAVE20",
  "provider": "Flipkart",
  "category": "Fashion",
  "discount": 10,
  "expiryDate": "2027-06-30"
}

### 4. Invalid body -> 400 Bad Request with a list of field errors
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "x",
  "provider": "",
  "discount": 150,
  "expiryDate": "2020-01-01"
}

### 5. List all coupons
GET {{baseUrl}}

### 6. Filter by category (case doesn't matter)
GET {{baseUrl}}?category=electronics

### 7. Get one coupon (paste an id from step 2 or 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/PASTE_ID_HERE

### 8. Update a coupon
PUT {{baseUrl}}/PASTE_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SAVE25",
  "provider": "Amazon",
  "category": "Electronics",
  "description": "Now 25% off!",
  "discount": 25,
  "expiryDate": "2027-12-31"
}

### 9. Delete a coupon -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/PASTE_ID_HERE

### 10. Get an id that doesn't exist -> 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist
